              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Gujarati for to hesitate, then the Gujarati for to waver."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: પાક",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "પાક — pāk — \"a crop\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "જો સમયસર વરસાદ પડશે તો આ વરસે પાક સારો થશે. jo samaysar varsād paḍśe to ā varse pāk sāro thaśe. If the rain comes on time, the crop will be good this year."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "પાક (pāk) shares its source with પાકવું (pākvũ), \"to ripen\": CDIAL traces both to Sanskrit pakvá, \"cooked, ripe\", which in the Atharvaveda already meant \"ripe corn\" (CDIAL 7621). CDIAL glosses the Gujarati noun only as \"sugar boiled for conserves\", so \"a crop\" is a sense it does not give."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "pāk",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *pāk*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "pāk, once more",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *pāk*, once more]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "jo samaysar varsād paḍśe to ā varse pāk sāro thaśe. — If the rain comes on time, the crop will be good this year.",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *jo samaysar varsād paḍśe to ā varse pāk sāro thaśe.* — If the rain comes on time, the crop will be good this year.]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "say the Gujarati for to hesitate, then the Gujarati for to waver, then say pāk again",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: say the Gujarati for to hesitate, then the Gujarati for to waver, then say *pāk* again]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 5,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
